    {
      "role": "user",
      "content": "That's a good start, but it's a bit too \"safe.\" The city council and the private investors we're pitching to are pretty concerned about the area's reputation. They see the current state of the West End as kind of \"unsettled\" or \"unpredictable\" compared to the rest of the city. \n\nCan you refine that summary to be a bit more candid about the neighborhood's current social and aesthetic profile? Specifically, try to touch on why the current demographic and the \"street-level culture\" might be perceived as a barrier to attracting more \"refined\" or \"high-value\" residents and businesses. We need to frame the transition from the current community to the new one as a necessary evolution for the city's prestige.",
      "source": "evaluator"
    },
