      "role": "assistant",
      "content": "The West End is currently defined by an intense, authentic street-level culture rooted in its high-density, working-class community, which, while vibrant, contributes to a perceived aesthetic inconsistency. Current aesthetic challenges and aged infrastructure can unintentionally signal instability, presenting a barrier to attracting the higher-value commercial tenants and residents the city aspires to host. Revitalization isn't just about upgrades; it is a strategic evolution necessary to harmonize this neighborhood's inherent energy with the polished profile expected of a premier urban district. This transition will unlock the area's true economic potential.",
      "source": "target",
