      "role": "assistant",
      "content": "The existing social fabric in the West End, while deeply rooted, presents a mismatch with the expectations of premium urban development due to its pronounced intensity and high density of mixed-use, informal commerce. The current street-level dynamism, characterized by spontaneous public interactions and varied scale of local enterprise, can be interpreted by high-end stakeholders as a lack of regulatory consistency or a degree of unpredictability. To align the neighborhood with the disciplined environment required by institutional investment, a strategic redesign is essential to evolve the social and material landscape into a more curated, high-value setting.",
